# The status line: DECSSDT (CSI Ps $ ~) and DECSASD (CSI Ps $ }). The engine has no status line:
# what a program writes to it is dropped, and the main display must not show it or be touched by it.

test text written to the status line is not drawn on the main display
spec VT510 manual DECSASD: selects the status line as the active display, where text goes (DECSSDT 2, host-writable); vttest 11/073 ("There should be TEXT IN THE STATUS LINE" once, on the status line)
size 40 3
feed \e[1;1H\e[2$~\e[1$}TEXT IN THE STATUS LINE\e[0$}There should be it
screen
|There should be it|
cursor 1,19

test cursor movement and editing in the status line leave the main display alone
spec VT510 manual DECSASD: the cursor moves to the selected display and stays there until the main display is selected; vttest 11/081 (cursor addressing in the status line)
size 40 3
feed main\e[2$~\e[1$}\e[2K\e[1G\e[1mfirst\e[5G\e[4mlast\r\n\eM\e[3;9H\e[2J\e[0$}!
screen
|main!|
cursor 1,6

test the main cursor and rendition come back as they were
spec VT510 manual DECSASD ("moves cursor to selected display area"); the main display's cursor is untouched while the status line is active
size 40 3
feed \e[2;5H\e[31m\e[2$~\e[1$}\e[3;9H\e[44m\e[0$}x
cursor 2,6
cell 2,5 text=x fg=idx:1 bg=default

test DECSASD 1 is ignored unless the status line is host-writable
spec VT510 manual DECSSDT and xterm ctlseqs DECSASD: "ignored unless the status line has been enabled by CSI 2 $ ~"
size 40 3
feed \e[1$}a\e[1$~\e[1$}b\e[0$~\e[1$}c
screen
|abc|

test a status line that stops being host-writable is no longer the active display
spec VT510 manual DECSSDT: only the host-writable line can be the active display
size 40 3
feed \e[2$~\e[1$}x\e[1$~y
screen
|y|

test reports and modes work while the status line is active
spec VT510 manual: DSR and the modes are not about a display
size 40 3
feed \e[2$~\e[1$}\e[5n\e[0$}
reply \e[0n

test DECRQSS tells the line's type and the active display
spec VT510 manual DECRQSS: DECSSDT answers `Ps $ ~` and DECSASD `Ps $ }`
size 40 3
feed \e[2$~\e[1$}\eP$q$}\e\\\eP$q$~\e\\
reply \eP1$r1$}\e\\\eP1$r2$~\e\\
